<title>USA: Columbia Gas Q3 shr loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Columbia Gas Q3 shr loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>RESTON, Va. 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr loss		   $0.11   profit	 $0.38</p>
<p> Net loss		   6,100   profit	19,300</p>
<p> Revs		     450,800		  366,300</p>
<p> Avg shrs	    55,200,000	     50,600,000</p>
<p>	  9  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr profit		 $2.88   profit	 $3.54</p>
<p> Net			153,400		  179,000</p>
<p> Revs		   2,236,200		1,851,600</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary53,300,000	     50,600,000</p>
<p>(All data above 000s)</p>
<p>NOTE - 1996 Q3 includes $2.5 million for the after-tax effect of severance and benefits expenses generated by an ongoing restructuring. 1995 Q3 included $8.5 million after-tax expense for bankruptcy-related issues and the benefit of not recording $42.9 million of interest prepetition debt during the Chapter 11 proceedings.</p>
<p>When adjusted, the company posted a 1996 Q3 loss of $0.07 per share versus a loss of $0.30 per share.</p>
<p>Full company name is Columbia Gas System Inc</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
